WEBVTT

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.100
Okay, here goes.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.330
Let's set off!

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:26.330
My, good morning, President Aria.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:40.230
Do you remember that day

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:50.730
When your heart suddenly began to race

00:00:54.890 --> 00:01:00.570
The rays from the blue sky were pouring over you...

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.750
...as you cut through the wind

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:11.590
I couldn't look away, and when our eyes met

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.420
I couldn't help but smile

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.100
It's just like a spiral

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:30.370
I want to spend my days waving to you

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:40.240
This is my proof that I was here with you

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.570
An eternal spiral

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:54.400
There's a path which stretches on ahead

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:03.150
When you climb the next hill,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.910
Let's meet again

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:12.770
Now Recruiting

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.260
I've asked the Gondola Association for applicants and put posters in public places.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.660
But of course, interviews and practical exams are indispensable!

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.670
Towards that faraway future...

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:37.720
It's my responsibility to carefully pick out the perfect new recruits for Aria Company.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.520
An application e-mail?

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.050
Look, President Aria, it's our first applicant!

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.650
She's from Manhome?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:58.000
But I only just finished sending the personnel request to the store.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.240
I haven't even updated the website yet,
so this is incredible timing.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:10.250
I-I-I-I'm sorry for jumping the gun!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.880
But why us?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:22.760
I've always wanted to be an Undine, and I just happened to see a photo of Aria Company on the Internet...

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:27.260
It felt like you were calling out to me.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:38.930
I know this is anything but "carefully picking out"
a recruit, but for some reason...

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:55.960
I was struck with the overwhelming impression that this was the girl we wanted.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:21.860
This view is something special.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:28.490
So have you two always looked up to Aika and Alice?

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.720
No, not really.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.530
If anything, I'd say the manager's obsessed with me.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:39.000
At Orange Planet, the company decides who apprentices get assigned to.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.840
So you don't get to choose for yourself...

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:48.450
Who you train under tends to be a pretty big deal.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:53.900
Even if they've got talent, some people quit because their mentor won't acknowledge it.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.310
Wow...

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.270
Which means that we...

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.970
have a duty to work hard so our good fortune doesn't go to waste!

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:05.320
Yes. This meeting was a blessing!

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.420
Let's all become Prima Undines together!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.790
President Aria!

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.040
Quick, grab the oar!

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.800
Gondola coming through!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.600
There's still so many things I don't know...

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.060
It's the same for us, too.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.730
The city's constantly changing.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:46.340
This system where Singles can take customers under a Prima's supervision didn't always exist, you know.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.320
Really?

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:57.100
Someone proposed it as a new form of training, and it gained traction until the system changed, a little bit at a time.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.960
I never knew.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:07.280
So many people I'll never know form the will of the city and support us from behind the scenes...

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.520
Could this be...

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.820
a sappy line?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:12.770
Huh?

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:16.020
Haha! Don't worry about it!

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.220
It sure got cloudy fast.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.890
Well, it's just that time of year.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.210
I'd say we're about due for an Acqua Alta.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.370
Acqua Alta...

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.690
Gondola coming through!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:53.680
Her smiles and songs soothe my soul.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.890
I know what you mean.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.350
You know...

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:04.020
Alice was really looking forward to Athena's special recital at the next music festival,

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:08.600
but apparently she suddenly got a job she couldn't refuse.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:14.820
Yeah, we got swamped too.
The manager can't even <i>think</i> of going.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.120
Our schedule is totally full.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.610
It's really too bad.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:23.960
Something the matter?

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.550
We should work a miracle!

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.420
Like, make one happen ourselves?

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.680
How?

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:36.270
The Acqua Alta! The Acqua Alta will bring us one!

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:40.150
Looks like she's in dreamer mode.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:41.780
You in?

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:44.190
You bet I'm in.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:17.180
All right! Look, President Aria, it's an Acqua Alta!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:20.960
Aqua's just so full of miracles!

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.010
Time to begin the operation!

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.980
Morning!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.990
Good morning, Akari!

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:31.650
It's an Acqua Alta today.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.940
Yes! That means today's jobs will get canceled, right?

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:35.820
Yeah.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:39.280
What do you say we relax away the time on the veranda?

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.600
No thank you!

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.320
I have somewhere I need to be.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.210
Then can we make pancakes for lunch together?

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.470
No!

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.840
I'm sorry, but I have plans for lunch, too.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.590
Then... I guess I'll get dinner ready while you're out.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.920
No. Please don't.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:03.260
I'll get in touch with you this evening, so just take it easy until then.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:05.560
Okay...

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:14.490
All right, you have your missions.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.980
I wish us all the best of luck!

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.180
Roger!

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:38.220
Aika and Alice already have plans today...

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.120
And Ai seems busy, too.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:48.610
Once everyone's schedules open up,
I want to go to those hot springs together.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:52.000
The ocean might be nice this time of year, too.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:58.740
And if possible, I hope Alicia and Grandma can come with us.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:06.570
I know these wishes will probably never come to pass,

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:10.800
but I just can't stop holding out hope.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:12.750
How mysterious.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.470
Oh, an e-mail.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.120
It's from Ai.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.850
Are you nice and rested?

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.520
Please be here at five. I'll be waiting!

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.860
This is...

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.080
Welcome, Akari!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.580
We've been expecting you!

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:05.850
Please, take a seat.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.720
A tea party?

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.870
Yes!

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:11.400
Is today a holiday, or something?

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.290
No, not at all.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.900
Having a party on just a normal day? That's so wonderful!

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.210
Huh? Junior?

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.360
Aika...

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:23.780
Here they are!

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.570
So the juniors called you here, too?

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:29.580
Yeah.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:32.290
Gee, I wonder what's going through their heads...

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.030
Aika! Alice!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.230
So this is why you said you had plans.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.590
You were busy getting this ready.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.380
It really was the perfect crime.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:57.100
It looks like you've got too many chairs, though.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.480
Yeah.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:02.300
Wait, did you...

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.030
You called Alicia and her friends, too?

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:06.950
Enough!

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:14.170
I understand your happiness,
but you should have said my name instead.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.370
My, my.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.840
Alicia! Grandma!

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.170
Thank you so much for the invitation.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.330
Wow!

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.400
Good job, you guys!

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:29.630
We wanted to express our gratitude for everything you do for us.

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:35.990
Athena said she'd finish her music festival practice as fast as she could so she can make it here.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:40.530
It would take a miracle for that to happen.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:44.520
Well, look how many people we have already.

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:47.240
Yes, even this much is quite the miracle.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.210
What a lovely smell. Is this rose tea?

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.150
Yes!

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:56.430
It's the smell of the miracle Ai and her friends gave us.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.080
No sappy lines allowed!

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.210
Huh?

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:09.490
Thank you. It was quite delicious.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:15.010
But Singles from three different companies making friends and practicing together again?

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:17.020
Fate works in mysterious ways.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.260
Yes, it certainly does.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:24.170
Never in my wildest dreams did I imagine my meeting with President Aria

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:29.950
would lead to something as wonderful as this.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:33.700
It's such a wonderful feeling.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.900
Really makes you excited for the future.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.880
Alicia...

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:47.660
She must be exhausted.
Changing the status quo is a hard thing to do.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:50.300
Changing the status quo...

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:57.230
She's trying to change the Prima system for the sake of future Undines.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:04.490
Some meetings can be happy,
but others close doors to the future.

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:12.670
She must be thinking that if the system put in place by the Gondola Association is the cause, she has to change that.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:14.400
I never knew...

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:20.780
Alicia knows better than any of us how important meetings are.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:31.850
Shortly after people started calling us the "Three Great Water Fairies,"

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:36.680
the Gondola Association made a request of us.

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:44.610
We politely declined, but they were persistent.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:52.640
They said it was for the sake of the Undines in ten, or even a hundred years from now,

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:55.580
arguing their point with impassioned vigor.

00:14:56.360 --> 00:15:02.290
Eventually, they got to me,
and I decided I wanted to give it a shot.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:09.960
The gentlemen from the Gondola Association said they'd wait for us, President Aria.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:16.920
They'll leave us alone until I can raise new Undines that I can trust with the company in busy times.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:20.280
New Undines...

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.860
"It felt like you were calling out to me."

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:34.990
Those imaginative words marked the beginning of my meeting with Akari.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:46.360
Go at your own pace, with no particular destination in mind.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:54.520
Grow at your own pace in the company you love, alongside this young girl.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:57.020
That was my decision.

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:02.020
What is this? It's so cute!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.690
It's a night-shine chime.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:07.180
Wow, I've never seen one before!

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:07.180
My, my. This is fun.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.900
Tante grazie.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.510
Wow...

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:27.690
As the seasons passed on Aqua,
you slowly became special to me.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:32.970
Those were the happiest of times.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:37.810
Precious, magical times.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:42.850
The daily life I took for granted and the way the world expressed itself

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.590
had begun to shine brighter than ever before.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:50.400
It was like you had cast a magic spell on me.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:55.670
I never wanted to lose this one-of-a-kind time.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.770
I wanted it to go on forever.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.410
If I could use magic spells too,

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.890
I'd want to freeze the flow of time.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.810
Oh, that's...

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:28.690
Yes, I brought it with me. It doesn't glow anymore, though.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:33.160
Akari?

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:37.610
How did you feel when it stopped glowing?

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:44.040
I felt lonely, very lonely.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.570
Goodbyes are always lonely.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:56.540
Even for this thing and the gondola, it was lonely and sad.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:04.100
But I think that's probably a good thing, Alicia.

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:15.850
The loneliness or sadness you feel when you say goodbye to something reflects how precious it was to you.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:21.200
It's something that will live on in you for as long as you live,

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:26.570
something that will continue to shine here on Aqua forever.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:34.920
That's why I think someone's sadness is proof of their happiness.

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:48.560
You were lifting the hesitation from my heart.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:59.210
You made me transparent and dyed me in your own unique colors.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:04.370
You were like the deep and distant blue sea that extends into the horizon

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.730
and envelops all of Aqua in its gentle embrace.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:12.110
Thank you, Akari.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.570
Akari says some interesting things, huh?

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:29.930
"Loneliness and sadness are proof of your happiness," was it? She has a point.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:35.170
Alice is about to graduate middle school, so we need to prepare ourselves.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:40.570
Besides the Gondola Association,
you've got someone else you're keeping waiting, right?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.110
Yeah.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.570
Everything's going perfectly for you.

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.790
No more hesitating, got it?

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.270
Yeah.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.430
It stopped raining.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.520
So, shall we begin?

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:12.920
Yes!

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.870
The magic is wearing off.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:22.400
Time had stopped for me, but now it's moving again.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.080
Good morning, sunshine.

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:30.370
Was I dreaming?

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.730
What were you dreaming about?

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.090
A meeting I cherish.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:43.810
I haven't relaxed this much in ages!

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:46.330
Thank you three for planning this.

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:50.740
Athena never did show up.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:53.520
Finishing the practice early was totally impossible to begin with.

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:56.020
I'm really not surprised.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:21:00.190
But you still left the seed of your wish.

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:03.160
The seed of our wish?

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:11.950
Yes, the seed of a wish that didn't come true remains in your heart and continues to shine with hope.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:18.460
Unless you get rid of it yourselves, you'll still feel the excitement.

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:22.960
And isn't that a happy thing?

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:27.340
So that's why people save up those seeds.

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:34.460
And the funny thing is,
sometimes wishes that are never meant to be

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:39.610
end up changing their forms and presenting themselves to you in new ways.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.950
It's an exciting feeling.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:50.220
Next time, let's make it so everyone can be here.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:53.240
Maybe we could have a gondola party.

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:54.830
Yeah!

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:15.790
The setting sun and the rippling waves

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:17.180
Athena!

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:35.240
Seem like a song of pure happiness

00:22:39.470 --> 00:22:56.120
The birds are like messengers, delivering kindness

00:22:56.780 --> 00:23:14.100
They fly beyond the sea, placing love on the winds

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:34.450
In the twilight sky, which makes my heart tremble,

00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:46.200
Lies a star of hope that will shine forevermore

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:43.570
It's really a miracle!

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:49.180
Today will go down in history as the day Ai and her friends worked a miracle.

00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:51.480
No sappy lines allowed.

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:56.420
We've been connected, ever since way back then.

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:57.310
Yes.

00:23:59.390 --> 00:24:07.550
The individual paths we walked joined together formed a new path, and then separated again.

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:11.520
Congratulations, Alice.

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:15.480
Or should I say...

00:24:15.480 --> 00:24:17.240
Orange Princess.

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:21.750
From this day forth, you are a Prima Undine!

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:25.270
I won't forgive you if you fail.

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:32.920
My future Queen.

00:24:34.220 --> 00:24:35.200
Right!

00:24:42.870 --> 00:24:46.610
I'm so glad that I met you.

00:24:48.230 --> 00:24:50.070
Thank you...

00:24:50.070 --> 00:24:51.970
my Aquamarine.

00:24:53.750 --> 00:24:55.640
Aquamarine...

00:24:57.620 --> 00:25:00.100
The distant, endless blue.

00:25:04.470 --> 00:25:07.020
I walked my path without stopping or hesitating,

00:25:07.020 --> 00:25:10.830
and that's why I was able to meet you.

00:25:12.110 --> 00:25:16.610
Now I'll continue walking...

00:25:16.610 --> 00:25:18.140
even as the times change.

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:27.680
I make a wish

00:25:28.310 --> 00:25:38.650
To the clouds vanishing beyond the calm blue

00:25:38.650 --> 00:25:42.990
Hoping for a new day to dawn on us

00:25:43.660 --> 00:25:51.460
Now, let's be on our way

00:25:51.920 --> 00:25:57.050
It's time for our journey to begin

00:25:58.170 --> 00:26:09.560
Let's set sail together

00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:18.070
And little by little, head toward our goal

00:26:18.070 --> 00:26:28.490
I realized that you always watched over me

00:26:28.490 --> 00:26:38.500
Though you might not be by my side anymore

00:26:38.500 --> 00:26:52.440
You taught me what happiness means

00:26:52.440 --> 00:26:59.190
I will never forget that

00:26:59.190 --> 00:27:11.750
And these feelings will shine eternal

00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:10.730
Now, let's set off...

00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:13.400
to a new future!
